        <h2>What is actinic keratosis?</h2>
        <p>Actinic keratosis is a rough, scaly patch of skin that is considered a precancer. Also called solar keratosis, these growths commonly show up on parts of the body that get a lot of sun, like the face, head, neck and hands. Actinic keratoses (plural) may present in different ways, and they often look like a crusty, scaly or dry area of skin.</p>
        <p>Actinic keratosis doesn’t mean you have cancer. But some of these patches can eventually turn into <a href="#">squamous cell skin cancer</a> if left untreated. Because of this possibility, having actinic keratosis increases your chances of developing skin cancer at some point in your life.</p>
